---
import PageLayout from '../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';
import FAQ from '../components/FAQ.astro';
import CTA from '../components/CTA.astro';
import ServiceSchema from '../components/ServiceSchema.astro';

const faqs = [
  { q: "Am I too old to start?", a: "No. We have students who started in their 50s and 60s. The art rewards technique over athleticism." },
  { q: "Will I get hurt?", a: "Risk exists in any physical activity. BJJ's injury rate is lower than most sports. We don't put new students in hard rolling. You set the pace." },
  { q: "Do I need to be in shape first?", a: "No. You'll get in shape by training. Starting fit helps, but it's not required." },
  { q: "How often should I train?", a: "Two to three times per week is ideal for adults over 40 — enough to progress, with enough recovery time." },
  { q: "Free trial?", a: "Two weeks, unlimited classes. No card, no contract. Call (908) 341-1131." },
];
---

<PageLayout
  title="BJJ Over 40 in Union, NJ — Starting BJJ After 40 | AllStar"
  description="Starting BJJ after 40 in Union, NJ at AllStar Martial Arts. Renzo Gracie black belt. Students in their 50s and 60s train here. Free 2-week trial — no contract."
  ogImage="/images/adult-bjj-hero.jpg"
>
  <Fragment slot="head">
    <ServiceSchema
      serviceName="BJJ for Adults 40+"
      serviceDescription="Brazilian Jiu-Jitsu classes specifically designed for adults over 40. Lower-impact, technique-focused training emphasizing longevity and enjoyment."
      serviceType="BJJ for Adults 40+"
      pageUrl="/bjj-over-40/"
    />
  </Fragment>
  <PageHero
    eyebrow="Adults 40+ Welcome"
    headline="Starting BJJ After 40 in Union, NJ"
    sub="It's not too late. Students in their 50s and 60s train here. Renzo Gracie lineage. Free 2-week trial — no contract, no pressure."
    bgImage="/images/adult-bjj-hero.jpg"
    programLocked="Adult BJJ"
  />

  <!-- Intro -->
  <section class="section-pad bg-white">
    <div class="container-page max-w-3xl">
      <p class="text-lg md:text-xl text-brand-gray leading-relaxed mb-5">
        We have students in their 50s and 60s who started after 40. One started at 52 after his doctor told him to find something low-impact. He's been on the mat for six years. He's in better shape than he was at 35.
      </p>
      <p class="text-lg md:text-xl text-brand-gray leading-relaxed">
        The thing most people get wrong about starting BJJ after 40: they assume the body won't cooperate. What actually happens is the opposite — BJJ rewards the qualities that come with age. Patience. Ability to focus. Comfort with discomfort. Willingness to think before reacting.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Why BJJ is good for 40+ -->
  <section class="section-pad bg-brand-gray-light">
    <div class="container-page max-w-4xl">
      <div class="eyebrow">Why BJJ works for adults over 40</div>
      <h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl text-brand-black mb-8">Five Reasons the Math Works in Your Favor</h2>
      <div class="space-y-5">
        <div class="bg-white p-6 rounded-lg shadow-sm">
          <h3 class="text-xl text-brand-black mb-2">Technique beats strength</h3>
          <p class="text-brand-gray leading-relaxed">This isn't a motivational slogan — it's how the art was designed. Helio Gracie built BJJ because he was a small, frail man who couldn't match bigger opponents physically. The art rewards leverage, timing, and position. All of which improve with experience, not youth.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-white p-6 rounded-lg shadow-sm">
          <h3 class="text-xl text-brand-black mb-2">No striking</h3>
          <p class="text-brand-gray leading-relaxed">BJJ is grappling only. There's no getting punched in the face. The injury rate is lower than soccer, basketball, or recreational running.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-white p-6 rounded-lg shadow-sm">
          <h3 class="text-xl text-brand-black mb-2">You set the pace</h3>
          <p class="text-brand-gray leading-relaxed">Nobody forces you to roll hard. You control intensity. Many older students train at 60–70% and get the full technical benefit without beating their body up.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-white p-6 rounded-lg shadow-sm">
          <h3 class="text-xl text-brand-black mb-2">The fitness benefit is real</h3>
          <p class="text-brand-gray leading-relaxed">Flexibility, core strength, cardiovascular health — BJJ builds all three without the joint damage of high-impact sports.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-white p-6 rounded-lg shadow-sm">
          <h3 class="text-xl text-brand-black mb-2">It compounds</h3>
          <p class="text-brand-gray leading-relaxed">A decade of BJJ builds into something real. Each year you're better than the last. The same can't be said for most fitness routines that plateau within months.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- What it looks like -->
  <section class="section-pad bg-brand-navy text-white">
    <div class="container-page max-w-4xl">
      <div class="eyebrow text-brand-gold">The real timeline</div>
      <h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl mb-8">What Starting BJJ Over 40 Actually Looks Like</h2>
      <div class="grid md:grid-cols-3 gap-6">
        <div class="bg-white/5 p-6 rounded-lg">
          <div class="font-display text-3xl text-brand-gold mb-2">Month 1–2</div>
          <p class="text-white/90 text-sm leading-relaxed">You feel awkward. You tap constantly. You leave sore. The movements start making sense by week four.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-white/5 p-6 rounded-lg">
          <div class="font-display text-3xl text-brand-gold mb-2">Month 3–6</div>
          <p class="text-white/90 text-sm leading-relaxed">You have a game — a set of positions and submissions you understand and can apply. Body comp improves without trying.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-white/5 p-6 rounded-lg">
          <div class="font-display text-3xl text-brand-gold mb-2">Year 2+</div>
          <p class="text-white/90 text-sm leading-relaxed">People half your age are having a harder time with you than they expected. The patience advantage is real and growing.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Coach's approach -->
  <section class="section-pad bg-white">
    <div class="container-page max-w-3xl">
      <div class="eyebrow">Coach Jamal's approach</div>
      <h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl text-brand-black mb-5">Coached for Your Body, Not a 22-Year-Old Competitor</h2>
      <p class="text-brand-gray leading-relaxed mb-4">
        Jamal has coached students over 40 for his entire career at AllStar. His take: they're often the best students in the room. They listen. They don't ego-trip. They show up consistently. And consistency is what BJJ rewards above everything else.
      </p>
      <p class="text-brand-gray leading-relaxed">
        He also knows where the bodies break down — knees, shoulders, backs. He adjusts. The curriculum at AllStar for older beginners isn't the same as for 22-year-old competitors. You'll be treated as an adult with a body worth taking care of.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <FAQ items={faqs} />

  <CTA
    headline="Two Weeks Free. Any Age."
    sub="BJJ after 40 in Union, NJ. Renzo Gracie lineage. Students in their 50s and 60s train here. Come see for yourself."
  />
</PageLayout>
